return {
["00:00"]={"Gately can hear the horns and raised voices and u-turn squeals way down below on Wash. That indicates it’s around \0030000h.\004, the switching hour.","Infinite Jest","David Foster Wallace"},
["00:01"]={"With the appointed execution time of \003one minute past midnight\004 just seconds away, I knocked on the metal door twice. The lock turned and the door swiftly swung open.","Death at Midnight","Donald A. Cabana"},
["00:02"]={"At \003two minutes past twelve\004 the door opens and two men come into the lobby. One is tall with black hair combed in a 50’s pompadour. The other is short and bespectacled. Both are wearing suits.","Billy Summers","Stephen King"},
["00:03"]={"It was just \003three minutes past midnight\004 when I last saw Archer Harrison alive. I remember, because I said it was two minutes past and he looked at his watch and said it was three minutes past.","Since Ibsen","George Jean Nathan"},
["00:04"]={"At \003four minutes past midnight\004, January 22, Admiral Lowry’s armada of more than 250 ships reached the transport area off Anzio. The sea was calm, the night was black.","Anzio: Epic of Bravery","Fred Sheehan"},
["00:05"]={"It was \003after twelve o’clock\004 when Easton came home. Ruth recognised his footsteps before he reached the house, and her heart seemed to stop beating when she heard the clang of the gate, as it closed after he had passed through.","The Ragged Trousered Philanthropists","Robert Tressell"},
["00:06"]={"At \003six minutes past midnight\004, death relieved the sufferer.","West of Hell’s Fringe","Glenn Shirley"},
["00:07"]={"It was \003seven minutes after midnight\004. The dog was lying on the grass in the middle of the lawn in front of Mrs. Shears’s house. Its eyes were closed. It looked as if it was running on its side, the way dogs run when they think they are chasing a cat in a dream.","The Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night-Time","Mark Haddon"},
["00:08"]={"Hour of the night! exclaimed the priest; “it is day, not night, and the hour is \003eight past midnight\004!”","The Brigantine","James Pascoe"},
["00:09"]={"At \00312:09 am\004 on 18 October, the cavalcade had reached the Karsaz Bridge, still ten kilometres from her destination.","The Bhutto Murder Trail: From Waziristan to GHQ","Amir Mir"},
["00:10"]={"At \003ten minutes past midnight\004 a call was made to the police by Garry Ashe from his aunt’s house to say that he had returned from a walk to discover her body.","A Certain Justice","P.D. James"},
["00:11"]={"The first incendiaries to hit St Thomas’s Hospital had splattered Riddell House at \003eleven minutes past midnight\004, from where a few hours earlier the Archbishop of Canterbury had given ‘an inspiring address’.","The Longest Night","Gavin Mortimer"},
["00:12"]={"It was \003twelve minutes past midnight\004 when mother and daughter saw the first lightning strike. It hit the main barn with such force the ground trembled under their feet.","Kentucky Heat","Fern Michaels"},
["00:13"]={"It’s \003thirteen minutes past midnight\004. We’re on yet another plane, this time from San Diego To Boston via Chicago. All around me people are sleeping.","Madlands","Anna Rose"},
["00:14"]={"It was exactly \003fourteen minutes past midnight\004 when he completed the final call. Among the men he had reached were honourable men. Their voices would be heard by the President.","The Matarese Circle","Robert Ludlum"},
["00:15"]={"At \003twelve-fifteen\004 he got out of the van. He tucked the pistol under the waistband of his trousers and crossed the silent, deserted street to the Hudston house.","Watchers","Dean Koontz"},
["00:16"]={"At \003sixteen minutes past midnight\004, Block 4 was hit and the roof set alight.","The Longest Night","Gavin Mortimer"},
["00:17"]={"So you deduce that I arrived at the fallen tree later than \003twelve seventeen a.m.\004 It may have been so. As I wasn’t concocting an alibi, I didn’t check the time every two minutes.","Shroud for a Nightingale","P.D. James"},
["00:18"]={"21st December 1985, \00312:18 a.m.\004\n[IN BED]\nMichael doesn’t believe in Heaven or Hell. He’s got closer to death than most living people and he tells me there was no tunnel of light or dancing angels. I’m a bit disappointed, to be honest.","The Book of Lies","Mary Horlock"},
["00:21"]={"\00312:21 A.M.\004\nUh-oh. Vance felt the tracks suddenly shiver. Then with what sounded like a painful grind of metal on metal, the gantry started moving again. They’d decided to override the safety shutoff.","Project Cyclops","Thomas Hoover"},
["00:22"]={"Nobody had been one of Mycroft Ward’s most important operatives and for sixty seconds every day, between 12:21 am and \00312:22 am\004, his laptop was permitted to connect directly with the gigantic online database of self that was Mycroft Ward’s mind.","The Raw Shark Texts","Steven Hall"},
["00:24"]={"Sanders with Sutton as his gunner began their patrol at \00312:24 am\004, turning south towards Beachy Head at 10,000 ft.","The Longest Night","Gavin Mortimer"},
["00:25"]={"I mean, look at the time! \003Twenty-five past midnight\004! It was a triumph, it really was!","The Soldier’s Wife","Joanna Trollope"},
["00:28"]={"The DRINK CHEER-UP COFFEE wall clock read \00312:28\004.","11/22/63","Stephen King"},
["00:29"]={"“What time is it?” asked Teeny-bits.\nThe station agent hauled out his big silver watch, looked at it critically and announced: “\003Twenty-nine minutes past twelve\004.”\n“Past twelve!” repeated Teeny-bits. “It can’t be.”","The Mark of the Knife","Clayton H. Ernst"},
["00:30"]={"“I love you more than you can possibly know.”\n“I love you too.” I smile and his lips linger on my cheek. As he walks down the hall, I note the time: \003half past midnight\004.","Bath Haus","P.J. Vernon"},
["00:31"]={"Third individual approaches unnoticed and without caution. Once within reach, individual reaches out toward subjects. Recording terminates: timecode: \00300:31\004:02.","Zombie Apocalypse! Fightback","Stephen Jones"},
["00:32"]={"Meticulously he noted the time by the wall clock over the fireplace and made a record in his book. “\00312:32\004 Mr. Courtney-Brigs reports fallen tree across the Winchester Road path.”","Shroud for a Nightingale","P.D. James"},
["00:33"]={"Stephen Maxie looked him straight in the eye and said almost casually: “It was \003thirty-three minutes past twelve\004 by my watch.”","Cover Her Face","P.D. James"},
["00:34"]={"\003Thirty-four minutes past midnight\004. ‘We got ten minutes to be back here.’ LT didn’t argue. Schoolboy knew his former trade. LT’s eyes fretted over the museum. ‘Not still worrying about the security, are you, because there ain’t none.’","Killer Tune","Dreda Say Mitchell"},
["00:35"]={"The clock read \003thirty-five minutes past midnight\004. I was dazed from the deepness of the sleep. Who could be calling me at this hour?","A Cat on the Cutting Edge","Lydia Adamson"},
["00:36"]={"The prosecutor looked at her gold watch. \003Thirty-six minutes past midnight\004.","The Frozen Dead","Bernard Minier"},
["00:37"]={"A glance at the luminous dial of his watch showed to be \003thirty-seven minutes past midnight\004.","Not a Marrying Man","Dixie Browning"},
["00:38"]={"You left the main hospital building at about midnight. You spoke to the porter at the main gate at \003twelve thirty-eight a.m.\004 Where were you between those times?","Shroud for a Nightingale","P.D. James"},
["00:39"]={"It was \00312:39 a.m.\004 and I watched the moon fall prey to an evil-looking pack of galloping dark clouds.","Monastery Nightmare","Ross H. Spencer"},
["00:40"]={"It was the opinion of the forensic pathologist who saw the body at \003twelve-forty\004 that Mrs. O’Keefe had died very shortly after her return home.","A Certain Justice","P.D. James"},
["00:41"]={"By the time he came back to his car, it was \00312:41 am\004. I was standing outside my car, just waiting and he noticed me.","Blood Ties","Geraldo Cruz"},
["00:43"]={"Died five minutes ago, you say? he asked. His eye went to the watch on his wrist. \003Twelve-forty-three\004, he wrote on the blotter.","A Pocket Full of Rye","Agatha Christie"},
["00:44"]={"It was \00312:44 A.M.\004 when she turned the corner by Brulee’s onto Stateline Road. She waited on the approaching train.","Burning Embers","Wayne Pearson"},
["00:45"]={"At \00312:45\004, during a lull, Mr. Yoshogi told me that owing to the war there were now many more women in England than men.","Pig and Pepper: A Comedy of Youth","David Footman"},
["00:46"]={"Teddy wrote that phone records confirm Miss Lutton’s story. She called at \00312:46 a.m.\004","Dial M for Mischief","Kasey Michaels"},
["00:47"]={"At \00312:47 a.m\004. Uncle Ho left us forever.","Last Night I Dreamed of Peace","Andrew X. Pham"},
["00:48"]={"Stanton shut the light off, glancing quickly at the clock’s red numerals; it was \00312:48 a.m.\004 She tried to remember what day it was.","The Moriah Ruse","Marvin Wiebener"},
["00:49"]={"That’s when they began yelling for help. A security guard at a nearby high-rise heard their cries and called police. It was \00312:49 A.M.\004 Metro-Dade Officer Bart Cohen and his partner arrived one minute later.","Never Let Them See You Cry","Edna Buchanan"},
["00:50"]={"The packing was done at \00312:50\004; and Harris sat on the big hamper, and said he hoped nothing would be found broken. George said that if anything was broken it was broken, which reflection seemed to comfort him. He also said he was ready for bed.","Three Men in a Boat","Jerome K. Jerome"},
["00:51"]={"My smile suddenly vanished after realizing the time. It was \00312:51\004 and at one in the morning usually checks us. I tried to run as fast as I could to reach the elevator until I did.","All the Stars Above Us","Jyerrmou"},
["00:52"]={"New Year’s Eve night, well, way early New Year’s morning, 1998\nLet’s be exact: Let’s say it was \00312:52 a.m.\004\nI discovered what I want:\nAttention.","The Year of Lovemaking & Crying","Kenneth Robinson"},
["00:53"]={"But he came out of it so slowly this time that Jacqueline had already picked up the phone and said hello before he was fully awake. The clock said it was \00312:53 A.M.\004 A bit early for Meade to call, yet who else could it be?","Impulse","Michael Weaver"},
["00:54"]={"Everybody was happy; everybody was complimentary; the ice was soon broken; songs, anecdotes, and more drinks followed, and the pregnant minutes flew. At \003six minutes to one\004, when the jollity was at its highest— BOOM! There was silence instantly.","A Double Barrelled Detective Story","Mark Twain"},
["00:55"]={"He rolled one way, rolled the other, listened to the loud tick of the clock, and was asleep a minute later. \003Five to one\004 in the morning. Fifty-one hours to go.","61 Hours","Lee Child"},
["00:56"]={"At \003twelve fifty-six A.M.\004, Jo O’Connor finally gave up on the idea of sleep. For hours she’d been awake worrying about Louis and Stormy and Sarah Two Knives. And about Cork.","Boundary Waters","William Kent Krueger"},
["00:57"]={"A minute had passed, and the roller dropped a new leaf. \00312:57\004. 12 + 57 = 69; 6 + 9 = 15; 1 + 5 = 6. 712 + 5 = 717; 71 + 7 = 78; 7 + 8 = 15; 1 + 5 = 6 again.","Lessons in Essence","Dana Standridge"},
["00:58"]={"It was downright shameless on his part to come visiting them, especially at night, \003almost at one in the morning\004, after all that had happened.","The Idiot","Fyodor Dostoyevsky"},
["00:59"]={"What time is it now? she said.\n“\003About one o’clock\004.”\n“In the morning?”\nHerera’s friend leered at her. “No, there’s a total eclipse of the sun.”","Freedom","Jonathan Franzen"},
